  "title": "Pair refinement determines the atoms",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Pair refinement determines the atoms (computed exactly on the 191 saved and 86 fresh maps, through the order-free far sides). Colour refinement (1-WL) on the native creation map puts lines of two different atoms in one class in 87 of 277 spaces, 14 of the 23 Fano trees among them; a canonical colouring cannot separate lines that a symmetry exchanges, so this is no obstruction. Pair refinement (folklore 2-WL, atomic types in both directions) never puts a pair within an atom and a pair across two atoms in one class, in all 277 spaces: the atom partition is a union of stable pair classes, so every automorphism of the native creation map maps atoms to atoms, and in each space 'same atom' is definable in three-variable counting logic. As a control, on the yes/no creation relation alone pair refinement mixes them in 42 spaces, including all 39 where lines of two atoms are yes/no twins (GLUE-READ C's obstruction).",
